<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kedu Plain</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kedu Plain is a fertile volcanic basin in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-java">Central Java</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, ringed by the volcanoes Merapi, Merbabu, Sumbing and Sindoro. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> fields supported the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medang-kingdom">Medang</a> kingdom and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sailendra-dynasty">Sailendra dynasty</a> in the eighth and ninth centuries, and it holds major monuments of that age, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borobudur">Borobudur</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mendut">Mendut</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pawon">Pawon</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kedu-plain.jpg" alt="Kedu Plain" width="320" height="115" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original uploader was Gunkarta at en.wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Borobudur_Panoramic_View.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
